Body:
In the latest version of the OpenCode GUI (1.2.17), I was able to add a custom provider under Settings. Adding a model is mandatory.

<img width="1435" height="962" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/44af9350-debb-400a-8b4c-d0c53f235151" />

<img width="1435" height="962" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/245bcea7-cb1a-4ede-a7c9-fcf38643e3a5" />

And this seems to work in the CLI and extensions as well. It updated `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`.

```
  "provider": {
    "bla": {
      "name": "Bla",
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "models": {
        "mistral:latest": {
          "name": "mistral:latest"
        },
        "gemma3:latest": {
          "name": "gemma3:latest"
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://bla.com/api/v1"
      }
    }
  }
```

Ahh, didn't know the 'v1' must be ommited. So this, as example, work for me (there is connection, no error for a promt):

```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "routster": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "Routster",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://api.routstr.com",
        "apiKey": "sk-<some_key>",
	"includeUsage": true
      },
      "models": {
        "kimi-k2.5": {
          "name": "kimi-k2.5",
          "limit": {
            "context": 262144,
            "output": 65535
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "model": "routster/kimi-k2.5"
}
```

But no $ usage is calculated.
